---
import DocShell from '../layouts/doc-shell.astro';
import { docsLinks } from '../lib/nav';
---

<DocShell
   title="Storybook usage"
   summary="Test Storybook components with the same applicability, driver, pattern, and verification commands you use for full pages. a11ied resolves story iframes automatically."
   links={docsLinks}
>
   <section>
      <h2>Example commands</h2>
      <pre><code>node packages/cli/dist/cli.js inspect applicable --storybook-url http://127.0.0.1:6006 --story-id forms-login--default --json
node packages/cli/dist/cli.js verify criterion 3.3.8 --storybook-url http://127.0.0.1:6006 --story-id forms-login--default --target virtual --json</code></pre>
      <p>
         The Storybook integration resolves the story to its iframe URL and carries the story identity
         through the result, so evidence stays tied to the specific component fixture you tested.
      </p>
      <p>
         For a broader overview, see the <a href="/workflows#agent-and-storybook">agent and Storybook workflow</a>.
      </p>
   </section>

   <section>
      <h2>Supported commands</h2>
      <ul>
         <li><code>inspect applicable</code> and <code>inspect criterion</code></li>
         <li><code>drive start</code> against a resolved story target</li>
         <li><code>run axe</code> and <code>run pattern</code></li>
         <li><code>verify criterion</code> and <code>verify level</code></li>
      </ul>
   </section>

   <section>
      <h2>When Storybook targets help</h2>
      <ul>
         <li>Testing isolated components like dialogs, forms, or live regions without a full app</li>
         <li>Using story metadata to inform applicability checks</li>
         <li>Running repeatable component-level tests while the full app is still in development</li>
      </ul>
   </section>

   <section class="field-note">
      <h2>Local dev server</h2>
      <p>
         The Storybook integration currently targets a local dev server you control. It is designed for
         component-level accessibility testing during development.
      </p>
   </section>
</DocShell>
